<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94749" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκευόφορ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carrying</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκεύη, ς. κάμηλοι</span>
			<i>baggage</i>-camels, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.80
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποζύγια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					4.1.24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					1.139
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ς</span>. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτήνη</span>) <i>pack-animals</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.79
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.4.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.</u>
				1.3.7
			</span></i>, al.: collectively in sg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶν τὸ
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.79.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.51.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.19.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst., of persons, <i>baggage-carrier, porter</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				497
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).121.79
			</span></i> (Epid., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PAmh.</u>
				2.62.13
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ς</span>.
				<i>sutlers, camp-followers</i>, esp. <i>the servants of the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλίτης</span>, who carried his baggage
			and shield, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ς. τε καὶ τὰ ὑποζύγια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.40
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
